{"title":"Career roadmap · Meteorologist","role":"Meteorologist","summary":"Career alignment: Meteorology is the scientific study of the atmosphere, weather systems, climate processes, forecasting, and atmospheric observations. A meteorologist combines physics, mathematics, atmospheric science, numerical modelling, satellite/radar observations, and data analysis to understand and predict weather.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For the specific target Meteorologist at IMD, the important point is that a B.Sc alone is generally not the endpoint. The roadmap should be designed around B.Sc → relevant PG qualification → competitive/recruitment pathway → IMD meteorological role, with the exact eligibility verified against the current official recruitment notification."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical role","Main focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Atmospheric Science Student"},{"text":"Physics + mathematics + atmospheric fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2–3"},{"text":"Weather/Climate Research Intern"},{"text":"Observation and data analysis"}],[{"text":"Graduate"},{"text":"Research / Weather Data Analyst"},{"text":"Atmospheric datasets"}],[{"text":"PG"},{"text":"Meteorology / Atmospheric Science Student"},{"text":"Advanced forecasting and modelling"}],[{"text":"Post-PG"},{"text":"Meteorologist / Scientific Officer pathway"},{"text":"Forecasting and atmospheric analysis"}],[{"text":"3–7 years"},{"text":"Meteorologist / Scientist"},{"text":"Operational forecasting/research"}],[{"text":"7–12+ years"},{"text":"Senior Scientist / Specialist"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction, climate, severe weather"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior Scientist / Technical Lead"},{"text":"Forecast systems, research and leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build during the B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Physics + mathematics foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Meteorology is highly quantitative, so the first priority is a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Physics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Waves"},{"text":"Radiation"},{"text":"Electricity and magnetism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Vector calculus"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Atmospheric fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Begin studying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Earth's atmosphere"},{"text":"atmospheric composition"},{"text":"pressure"},{"text":"temperature"},{"text":"humidity"},{"text":"wind"},{"text":"clouds"},{"text":"precipitation"},{"text":"solar radiation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"Jupyter"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Atmospheric science"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop deeper understanding of atmospheric processes."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atmospheric thermodynamics"},{"text":"Physical meteorology"},{"text":"Dynamic meteorology"},{"text":"Climatology"},{"text":"Synoptic meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric physics"},{"text":"Boundary-layer meteorology"},{"text":"Cloud physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand relationships such as"},{"type":"flow","items":["Temperature","Pressure","Density","Atmospheric Motion","Weather Systems"]},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"air masses"},{"text":"fronts"},{"text":"cyclones"},{"text":"anticyclones"},{"text":"convection"},{"text":"thunderstorms"},{"text":"monsoons"},{"text":"jet streams"},{"text":"atmospheric stability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Forecasting + atmospheric data"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the degree should become strongly career-oriented."},{"type":"h","text":"Weather observation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"surface observations"},{"text":"radiosondes"},{"text":"weather stations"},{"text":"weather radar"},{"text":"satellites"},{"text":"aircraft observations"},{"text":"ocean observations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Synoptic meteorology"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to interpret:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"weather maps"},{"text":"pressure systems"},{"text":"wind fields"},{"text":"temperature fields"},{"text":"humidity fields"},{"text":"satellite imagery"},{"text":"radar imagery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic concept:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Atmospheric Observations","Data Assimilation","Numerical Weather Model","Model Forecast","Meteorological Analysis","Weather Forecast"]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to develop a full weather model during B.Sc, but you should understand the underlying mathematics and computational workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Programming and data analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"A modern meteorologist should be comfortable working with large datasets."},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"xarray"},{"text":"Cartopy"},{"text":"Jupyter"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Geospatial/weather data"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NetCDF"},{"text":"GRIB"},{"text":"CSV"},{"text":"raster data"},{"text":"time-series datasets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data sources to practise with"},{"type":"p","text":"Use publicly available:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"weather observations"},{"text":"satellite datasets"},{"text":"reanalysis datasets"},{"text":"climate datasets"},{"text":"model forecast datasets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-year project"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a project involving real atmospheric data."},{"type":"h","text":"Strong project example"},{"type":"h","text":"“Analysis of Extreme Rainfall and Atmospheric Conditions Using Historical Weather Data”"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Weather Dataset","Data Cleaning","Exploratory Analysis","Rainfall / Temperature Trends","Atmospheric Variables","Statistical Analysis","Visualisation","Weather/Climate Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Other strong projects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Monsoon rainfall variability"},{"text":"Urban heat-island analysis"},{"text":"Cyclone-track analysis"},{"text":"Extreme temperature analysis"},{"text":"Thunderstorm prediction using ML"},{"text":"Air-pressure and rainfall relationship"},{"text":"Satellite-based cloud analysis"},{"text":"Atmospheric temperature profiling"},{"text":"Seasonal forecasting analysis"},{"text":"Machine learning for rainfall prediction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4-year Honours / advanced variant"},{"type":"p","text":"If the B.Sc offers an honours/research pathway, use the additional depth for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced atmospheric physics"},{"text":"Dynamic meteorology"},{"text":"Numerical methods"},{"text":"Atmospheric modelling"},{"text":"Climate dynamics"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"Radar meteorology"},{"text":"Data assimilation"},{"text":"Scientific computing"},{"text":"Machine learning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A research-oriented honours project can strengthen applications to M.Sc./M.Tech. programmes and atmospheric research internships."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Career direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"Synoptic Meteorology"},{"text":"Weather forecasting"}],[{"text":"Dynamic Meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric dynamics"}],[{"text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"text":"Weather modelling"}],[{"text":"Satellite Meteorology"},{"text":"Satellite-based observation"}],[{"text":"Radar Meteorology"},{"text":"Severe-weather monitoring"}],[{"text":"Climate Science"},{"text":"Climate analysis"}],[{"text":"Atmospheric Physics"},{"text":"Atmospheric research"}],[{"text":"Tropical Meteorology"},{"text":"Monsoon/cyclone research"}],[{"text":"Aviation Meteorology"},{"text":"Aviation weather"}],[{"text":"Agricultural Meteorology"},{"text":"Weather and agriculture"}],[{"text":"Marine Meteorology"},{"text":"Ocean-atmosphere systems"}],[{"text":"Air Quality / Atmospheric Chemistry"},{"text":"Pollution and atmospheric processes"}],[{"text":"Computational Meteorology"},{"text":"Weather data and modelling"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For the specific IMD Meteorologist pathway, a particularly strong combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Dynamic Meteorology","Synoptic Meteorology","Numerical Weather Prediction","Atmospheric Physics","Programming"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1–2"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for opportunities in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"atmospheric research"},{"text":"climate research"},{"text":"weather observation"},{"text":"environmental monitoring"},{"text":"university atmospheric-science laboratories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"flow","items":["data collection","physics","scientific analysis"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3"},{"type":"p","text":"Target projects involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"weather datasets"},{"text":"satellite imagery"},{"text":"climate data"},{"text":"rainfall analysis"},{"text":"numerical models"},{"text":"atmospheric observations"},{"text":"remote sensing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful organisations/research environments"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore opportunities associated with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"India Meteorological Department"},{"text":"Ministry of Earth Sciences institutions"},{"text":"IITs"},{"text":"IISERs"},{"text":"IISc"},{"text":"NCESS"},{"text":"NCPOR"},{"text":"other atmospheric/ocean/climate research laboratories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Availability and eligibility vary by institution, so check the current programme or internship notification."}]},{"heading":"Certifications and learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certificates are secondary to mathematical and scientific competence."},{"type":"h","text":"High-value learning areas"},{"type":"h","text":"Meteorology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Dynamic meteorology"},{"text":"Synoptic meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric thermodynamics"},{"text":"Climatology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"scientific computing"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Git"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"time-series analysis"},{"text":"data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Geospatial"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"remote sensing"},{"text":"satellite data analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"text":"WRF"},{"text":"data assimilation"},{"text":"machine learning for weather"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"type":"p","text":"If you want to become a modern computational meteorologist, eventually learn the basics of models such as WRF (Weather Research and Forecasting model)."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Initial Conditions","Atmospheric Model","Numerical Integration","Forecast Fields","Post-processing","Meteorological Interpretation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The important undergraduate objective is understanding what the model is doing and how to interpret its output, rather than simply learning commands."}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After B.Sc + relevant skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weather Data Analyst"},{"text":"Climate Data Analyst"},{"text":"Atmospheric Research Assistant"},{"text":"Weather Research Intern"},{"text":"Environmental Data Analyst"},{"text":"Remote Sensing Analyst"},{"text":"Meteorological Data Assistant"},{"text":"Climate Research Assistant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"After relevant PG qualification:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meteorologist"},{"text":"Atmospheric Scientist"},{"text":"Weather Forecaster"},{"text":"Climate Scientist"},{"text":"Numerical Weather Prediction Scientist"},{"text":"Satellite Meteorologist"},{"text":"Radar Meteorologist"},{"text":"Research Scientist"},{"text":"Atmospheric Data Scientist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What employers/recruiters may test"},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Be comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"calculus"},{"text":"differential equations"},{"text":"vectors"},{"text":"statistics"},{"text":"probability"},{"text":"numerical methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Expect:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"thermodynamics"},{"text":"fluid mechanics"},{"text":"radiation"},{"text":"heat transfer"},{"text":"atmospheric physics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Meteorology"},{"type":"p","text":"Know:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pressure systems"},{"text":"atmospheric stability"},{"text":"fronts"},{"text":"cyclones"},{"text":"convection"},{"text":"monsoons"},{"text":"clouds"},{"text":"precipitation"},{"text":"jet streams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forecasting"},{"type":"p","text":"Be able to interpret:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"synoptic charts"},{"text":"satellite images"},{"text":"radar data"},{"text":"upper-air observations"},{"text":"model forecast maps"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Python-based data analysis is increasingly useful:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Python","NumPy / pandas","xarray","NetCDF / GRIB","Atmospheric Dataset","Analysis + Visualisation"]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For the stated career target, PG study is a critical stage."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"p","text":"M.Sc."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"Atmospheric Physics"},{"text":"Geophysics"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Climate Science"},{"text":"Earth Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"M.Tech / specialised programmes"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on eligibility:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"Meteorology"},{"text":"Climate Science"},{"text":"Earth System Science"},{"text":"Remote Sensing"},{"text":"Geoinformatics"},{"text":"Environmental Science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact subject/degree eligibility for IMD recruitment varies by post and notification, so the current official recruitment advertisement should always be checked before selecting a PG programme."},{"type":"h","text":"IMD pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"For this specific row, the roadmap should be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Meteorology / Atmospheric Science","Strong Mathematics + Physics","M.Sc / relevant PG","Meteorology specialisation","Weather / climate research experience","Apply through applicable IMD recruitment pathway","Meteorologist / Scientific role"]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not assume that every B.Sc Meteorology graduate automatically qualifies for every IMD scientific post. Recruitment eligibility is post-specific, so verify the current official IMD/Ministry of Earth Sciences notification."}]},{"heading":"Study abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong postgraduate areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"Climate Science"},{"text":"Atmospheric Physics"},{"text":"Earth System Science"},{"text":"Computational Geoscience"},{"text":"Environmental Data Science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential destinations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Switzerland"},{"text":"Japan"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful international specialisations"},{"type":"h","text":"Weather"},{"type":"p","text":"→ Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"type":"h","text":"Climate"},{"type":"p","text":"→ Climate modelling"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"→ Remote sensing + satellite meteorology"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"p","text":"→ AI/ML + atmospheric science"}]},{"heading":"Career progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Operational meteorology"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc","Relevant PG","Meteorological Trainee / Entry-level Scientist","Meteorologist","Senior Meteorologist / Scientist","Senior Specialist","Technical / Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc","M.Sc","Research Assistant","PhD","Atmospheric Scientist","Senior Scientist","Principal Scientist / Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Computational pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc","M.Sc Atmospheric Science","Python + NWP + Data Science","Weather Data / NWP Analyst","NWP Scientist","AI Weather / Climate Scientist","Research / Technical Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD / research directions"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"text":"Monsoon dynamics"},{"text":"Tropical meteorology"},{"text":"Cyclone prediction"},{"text":"Severe weather"},{"text":"Climate modelling"},{"text":"Atmospheric convection"},{"text":"Cloud physics"},{"text":"Atmospheric radiation"},{"text":"Boundary-layer meteorology"},{"text":"Weather extremes"},{"text":"Climate change"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"Radar meteorology"},{"text":"Data assimilation"},{"text":"AI weather forecasting"},{"text":"Physics-informed machine learning"},{"text":"Coupled atmosphere-ocean modelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 career evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Meteorology is likely to become increasingly computational."},{"type":"h","text":"1. AI weather forecasting"},{"type":"p","text":"Machine-learning systems will increasingly complement traditional numerical models for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"precipitation prediction"},{"text":"cyclone forecasting"},{"text":"extreme-weather detection"},{"text":"downscaling"},{"text":"bias correction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. High-resolution forecasting"},{"type":"p","text":"Forecasting will increasingly move toward:"},{"type":"flow","items":["global","regional","local","neighbourhood-scale"]},{"type":"p","text":"predictions."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Satellite + radar + AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Future meteorologists will increasingly combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Satellite","Radar","Ground Stations","NWP","AI"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"for near-real-time forecasting."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Climate-risk analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Meteorological expertise will increasingly be applied to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"agriculture"},{"text":"infrastructure"},{"text":"renewable energy"},{"text":"aviation"},{"text":"disaster management"},{"text":"insurance"},{"text":"water resources"},{"text":"urban planning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. AI + physics"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile will not simply be an AI specialist."},{"type":"p","text":"It will be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Atmospheric Scientist","Physicist","Data Scientist"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Atmospheric science"},{"type":"p","text":"Meteorology"},{"type":"p","text":"Atmospheric Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Dynamic Meteorology"},{"type":"p","text":"Synoptic Meteorology"},{"type":"p","text":"Climatology"},{"type":"p","text":"Atmospheric Thermodynamics"},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics & physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Calculus"},{"type":"p","text":"Differential Equations"},{"type":"p","text":"Linear Algebra"},{"type":"p","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Probability"},{"type":"p","text":"Fluid Mechanics"},{"type":"p","text":"Thermodynamics"},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"NumPy"},{"type":"p","text":"pandas"},{"type":"p","text":"SciPy"},{"type":"p","text":"xarray"},{"type":"p","text":"matplotlib"},{"type":"p","text":"Linux"},{"type":"p","text":"Git"},{"type":"h","text":"Weather data"},{"type":"p","text":"NetCDF"},{"type":"p","text":"GRIB"},{"type":"p","text":"Reanalysis Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Satellite Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Radar Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Weather Station Data"},{"type":"h","text":"Modelling"},{"type":"p","text":"Numerical Weather Prediction"},{"type":"p","text":"WRF"},{"type":"p","text":"Numerical Methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Data Assimilation"},{"type":"p","text":"Model Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"p","text":"Remote Sensing"},{"type":"p","text":"Machine Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Deep Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Climate Modelling"},{"type":"p","text":"AI Weather Forecasting"},{"type":"p","text":"High-Performance Computing"},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Sc Meteorology / Atmospheric Science"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physics + Mathematics","Atmospheric Science","Python + Scientific Computing","Weather Observation + Synoptic Meteorology","Satellite/Radar Data","Numerical Weather Prediction","M.Sc / Relevant PG","Meteorological Research / Forecasting Experience","IMD Recruitment Pathway","Meteorologist","Senior Meteorologist / Scientist","Specialist / Research Lead","Senior Scientist / Technical Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For Meteorologist (IMD after PG), the strongest roadmap is not simply “B.Sc → IMD.” Build a quantitatively strong B.Sc foundation, then pursue a relevant postgraduate qualification with substantial meteorology/atmospheric-science content, while developing Python, numerical methods, weather-data analysis, satellite/radar interpretation and Numerical Weather Prediction. Always verify the current IMD recruitment notification and exact PG eligibility for the post you intend to target."},{"type":"table","header":["ID","Level","Category","Degree","Course","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"746"},{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Science"},{"text":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)"},{"text":"Meteorology / Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"Climate Data Analyst"}]]}]}]}